# The catch ball: red over a dark band over white.
# Y is up, +Z is the way the creature faces, one world unit is one map tile.
# The lowest vertex sits on y = 0 and the model is centred on x = 0 and z = 0,
# so the game places it by its feet.
#
# Faces are wound so that (c - a) x (b - a) points out of the solid, which is
# what tools/obj2cpp.py bakes as the face normal. Get it backwards and the
# model still draws, it just goes flat ambient dark.
#
# Eyes are not modelled. They are two depth tested dots in the 2D layer, which
# is a pixel each instead of eight triangles.
#
# 0.44 units across, 24 triangles.
# It follows the feet rule like everything else, so its origin is the
# point it rests on and a thrown ball's arc is the arc of its
# contact point, not of its centre.

mtllib ball.mtl

# shell, 24 triangles
v 0.000 0.440 0.000
v 0.191 0.330 0.000
v 0.095 0.330 0.165
v -0.095 0.330 0.165
v -0.191 0.330 0.000
v -0.095 0.330 -0.165
v 0.095 0.330 -0.165
v 0.191 0.110 0.000
v 0.095 0.110 0.165
v -0.095 0.110 0.165
v -0.191 0.110 0.000
v -0.095 0.110 -0.165
v 0.095 0.110 -0.165
v 0.000 0.000 0.000
usemtl ball_top
f 1 2 3
f 1 3 4
f 1 4 5
f 1 5 6
f 1 6 7
f 1 7 2
usemtl ball_band
f 2 8 9 3
f 3 9 10 4
f 4 10 11 5
f 5 11 12 6
f 6 12 13 7
f 7 13 8 2
usemtl ball_base
f 8 14 9
f 9 14 10
f 10 14 11
f 11 14 12
f 12 14 13
f 13 14 8
